{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R4"],
      "pins": ["R4.1", "R4.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R4 value field is '24k' and the SPICE deck uses 24k, but the MPN 'FRC0805J240TSD' and description '24Ω' indicate a 24Ω resistor.",
      "expected": "R4 should be 24kΩ as indicated by the value and its role as a bleeder across the PoE rails VOUTP/VOUTN; the BOM must match the intended 24kΩ value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R4\") (value \"24k\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R4 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the 24Ω MPN part is fitted, R4 will draw excessive current from the PoE output (VOUTP/VOUTN), dissipating tens of watts and likely damaging the board or loading the PoE source.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U17"],
      "pins": ["U17.6", "U17.8", "U17.9", "U17.12"],
      "nets": ["NET0195", "NET0192", "NET0076", "NET0169"],
      "observed": "U17 value and libsource are 'CC56-12SEKWA' (common cathode), but the MPN is 'FJ5461AH' (common anode) and the footprint is 'Display_7Segment:CA56-12SEKWA' (common anode). The description explicitly says 'Common cathode'.",
      "expected": "The value, footprint, and MPN should agree. The circuit uses a symbol with common-cathode pin names (CC1-CC4) and likely requires a common-cathode display, so the BOM/footprint should be for a CC56-12SEKWA or equivalent common-cathode part.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U17\") (value \"CC56-12SEKWA\") (footprint \"Display_7Segment:CA56-12SEKWA\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FJ5461AH\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" Red 4Bit Common cathode 0.56 Plugin LED Segment Displays ROHS\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the common-anode FJ5461AH is fitted, the ET6226M driver (if configured for common cathode) will not light the display correctly or may invert the display.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain at least two component identity/value anomalies: R4's value (24k) conflicts with its BOM MPN/description (24Ω), and U17's common-cathode value conflicts with its common-anode MPN and footprint. Both would cause the built board to behave differently from the intended design."
}

